OFFICIAL RELEASES ARE SIGNED
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Tanur is a censorship-circumvention tool. Hostile parties have an incentive to
distribute trojaned builds under its name. Protect yourself:

  * Official releases are cryptographically signed and published ONLY through
    the official channel:

        OFFICIAL_RELEASE_CHANNEL_PLACEHOLDER
        (set to the real URL/handle before the first public release)

  * Every official release ships a SHA256SUMS file and a detached signature
    over it. Verify both before running a binary. See RELEASING.md for the
    exact commands and the signing public key.

  * A build obtained from any other source, or one whose checksum or signature
    does not verify, should be treated as hostile. Do not run it.

If you redistribute Tanur (as MPL-2.0 permits), please make clear that your
build is not the official signed release, so users can tell the difference.

